Three decks, three systems
  MARSEILLE (18th c.) .... historical root; geometric pips;
                               adopted by esotericists, not designed by them
  RIDER-WAITE-SMITH (1909)  Golden Dawn teachings made visible;
                               illustrated minors; Waite reticent (oaths)
  THOTH (1940s/1969) ...... Crowley's Thelema via Frieda Harris;
                               renamed trumps; densest symbolism
  Rule: learn one deck's system completely before comparing;
        never mix attributions across decks unknowingly.

Golden Dawn founding (the documented and the claimed)
  DOCUMENTED: 1888, London; Westcott, Mathers, Woodman;
               Isis-Urania Temple No. 3; graded curriculum;
               Knowledge Lectures; 0=0 to 5=6 system.
  CLAIMED:    Cipher Manuscripts (Trithemian cipher) found via
               Rev. A.F.A. Woodford's papers; charter from
               'Fraulein Sprengel' of a German Rosicrucian order.
  STATUS:     documents exist; German order never verified;
               Sprengel letters disputed (forgery alleged).
  Built anyway: the Western tradition's standard curriculum.

Placing The Kybalion
  CLAIMED: ancient Hermetic teaching, 'Three Initiates'
  EVIDENCE: style/vocabulary match William Walker Atkinson;
            New Thought content (mind-power metaphysics);
            no pre-1908 trace of its distinctive doctrines;
            Atkinson's multi-persona publishing pattern fits.
  VERDICT: 1908 New Thought in Hermetic dress (Deslippe et al.)
  USE:      systematic modern teaching -- valuable if read as
            what it is, misleading if read as ancient transmission.

First-order vs second-order cybernetics
  FIRST-ORDER (Wiener): observer OUTSIDE the system;
     feedback loops in machines/organisms; control engineering.
  SECOND-ORDER (von Foerster): observer INSIDE the system;
     observing changes the observed; models construct systems;
     reflexivity replaces objectivity.
  The move: from 'how does the thermostat work?'
            to 'what does modeling thermostats do to us?'
